.* Rendering: a help module long enough to page, with every block kind.
:PNLGRP.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=WNAME CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='GADGET'.
:KEYL NAME=KEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=DUMMY KEYL=KEYS HELP=HLPWDG.Widgets
:TEXT DEPTH=2.
A panel so the group has one.
:ETEXT.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPWDG.Widgets - Help
:P.The Work with Widgets panel lists the widgets of a library and lets
you change, remove, show and describe them. Type an option next to an
entry and press Enter; the option runs for every entry you marked, in
the order of the list.
:H1.How to pick an entry
:P.Type the option number in the Opt column of the entry. To run the
same option for several entries, type it next to each of them. The
cursor's entry is &WNAME. when nothing is typed.
:P.To run a command instead, type it on the command line and press
Enter.  For help on a command, type its name and press F4 (Prompt).
:H2.Options
:UL.
:LI.Change: the change panel for the entry.
:LI.Remove: the entry is removed after you confirm.
:LI.Show: the display panel for the entry.
:EUL.
:H2.Keys
:DL.
:DT.F5
:DD.Refreshes the list from the library.
:DT.F11
:DD.Shows the quantities instead of the text.
:EDL.
:NT.Options you type stay on the panel until they run.
:ENT.
:H2.Examples
:XMP.
  2  GADGET     QGPL
  4  SPROCKET   QGPL
:EXMP.
:P.Marking :HP2.two:EHP2. entries runs both options when you press Enter.
See :LINK PERFORM='DSPHELP HLPMORE'.more about widgets:ELINK. for the rest.
:PARML.
:PT.LIB
:PD.The library whose widgets are listed.
:EPARML.
:OL.
:LI.First step.
:LI.Second step.
:EOL.
:P.The last paragraph ends the module after the page break.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPMORE.More About Widgets
:P.Widgets hold other widgets when their holds flag is on.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
